Lab 8: Containerized Node.js and MySQL Stack Using Docker Compose
1. Clone the application
bash
git clone https://github.com/Ibrahim-Adel15/iVolveApp.git
cd iVolveApp

The app needs a MySQL connection and a database named ivolve.

2. docker-compose.yml
yaml
services:
  app:
    build: .
    container_name: ivolve-app
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    environment:                    
      DB_HOST: db
      DB_USER: root
      DB_PASSWORD: rootpass
      DB_NAME: ivolve
    volumes:
      - app_logs:/app/logs
    networks:
      - ivolve-net
   
  db:
    image: mysql:8
    container_name: ivolve-db
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: rootpass
      MYSQL_DATABASE: ivolve
    volumes:
      - db_data:/var/lib/mysql
    networks:
      - ivolve-net
    
networks:
  ivolve-net:
    driver: bridge

volumes:
  app_logs:
  db_data:
3. Start and verify
bash
docker compose up -d --build
docker compose ps
docker compose logs -f app

Check the DB connection and database:

bash
docker exec -it ivolve-db mysql -uroot -prootpass -e "SHOW DATABASES;"

Open http://localhost:3000 and test the app.

Check persistence:

bash
docker compose down        # keeps volumes
docker compose up -d
docker volume ls
4. Build, tag and push to Docker Hub
bash
docker login
docker build -t medomeneam/ivolve-app:v1 .
docker push medomeneam/ivolve-app:v1
